---
description: Log console.error when bailing because a required value is missing
globs: frontend/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Log missing required values

When a function returns early because a required DOM node, lookup result, or
argument is null/undefined, call `console.error` first. Silent
`if (x === null) return` hides broken markup and wiring.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
if (element === null) return;

// ✅ GOOD
if (element === null) {
  console.error(`MediaEntry: #video${media.index} does not exist`);
  return;
}
```

Match existing messages: `` `${ClassName}: #${id} does not exist` ``.

Do not log again at a caller that already received null from a function that
logged (for example `PageElement.resolve()`, `Modal.child()`,
`MediaEntry.fromIndex()`).

Do not log expected control flow: type dispatch (`fromSaveElement` on the wrong
row kind), optional page features (`#carousel` on the day page), form values
that are allowed to be absent, or "already at the boundary" cases (move up
when the row is first).
